%% SEQ-07: Watchdog inhibit and guarded rollback
%% Behavior trace is in 02_Requirements/AIOS_Requirement_Behavior_Traceability.csv
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant WD as Independent Watchdog
    participant RT as Runtime Services
    participant POL as Policy Gate
    participant ACT as Actuator
    participant K as cgroups v2 controls
    participant AUD as Append-only Audit DB
    WD->>RT: Check heartbeat and input freshness independently
    RT--xWD: Missed heartbeat, stale evidence or unsafe health
    WD->>POL: Latch inhibit, reject new OS writes
    WD->>ACT: Request fallback for recorded AIOS changes
    ACT->>ACT: Verify cgroup identity and AIOS ownership
    alt CPU/RAM target identity matches
        ACT->>K: Restore captured prior value
        ACT->>K: Read back and verify
    else I/O target and device both match
        ACT->>K: Restore prior value for same device
        ACT->>K: Read back and verify
    else Identity or ownership fails
        ACT-->>WD: Do not write, flag review
    end
    WD->>AUD: Append trigger, inhibit and recovery evidence
    Note over WD,K: Linux native scheduling and memory management remain authoritative
